  "id": "antipathy",
  "term": "antipathy",
  "definition": "Antipathy is a strong, deep-rooted dislike toward some object, usually another person, that is felt as unreasoning or hard to explain. In this historical source, it is described as more intense than ordinary aversion and as arising either from associations of ideas or from inherited predisposition.",
